---
source: crates/deino-export/src/subtitles.rs
expression: srt(&export)
---
1
00:00:00,696 --> 00:00:06,531
Shreyas: Morning, everyone. Let's keep it quick today, I've got a hard stop at quarter to.

2
00:00:06,842 --> 00:00:09,302
Shreyas: Maya, do you want to kick us off?

3
00:00:09,764 --> 00:00:16,799
Maya Chen: Sure. So yesterday I mostly watched the Fernhollow dashboards after the dedupe fix went out on Tuesday.

4
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:25,508
Maya Chen: Zero new duplicates in two days, and Owen confirmed the same on his side this morning. So I'm calling the incident closed.

5
00:00:26,201 --> 00:00:29,001
Shreyas: Nice. That's a big one. Thank you.

6
00:00:29,630 --> 00:00:41,225
Maya Chen: Today I'm back on Calendar Sync v2, writing the subscription renewal part of the design doc. No blockers. And, uh, first morning off the pager, which is lovely.

7
00:00:41,595 --> 00:00:44,425
Shreyas: Well earned. Okay, Diego, you're up.

8
00:00:45,056 --> 00:00:52,926
Diego Alvarez: Yeah. Yesterday I got the read-only offline job list caching working on Android. Today I'm starting the iOS side.

9
00:00:53,246 --> 00:01:03,916
Diego Alvarez: I am kind of blocked, though. I need a last modified at field on each job in the jobs list endpoint, so the app knows when its cached copy is stale.

10
00:01:04,070 --> 00:01:13,765
Diego Alvarez: Right now I'm diffing the whole payload, which works, but it's slow and it's going to be terrible on a bad connection out in somebody's basement.

11
00:01:14,351 --> 00:01:21,116
Maya Chen: Oh, that one's on me, sorry. I said I'd add it last week and then the incident ate the week.

12
00:01:21,469 --> 00:01:26,789
Maya Chen: It's a small change. I can have it on the endpoint by end of day tomorrow.

13
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:31,105
Diego Alvarez: Tomorrow works. I'll stub it on my side until then.

14
00:01:31,485 --> 00:01:42,970
Diego Alvarez: For context, the Android cache keeps the next fourteen days of jobs for the technician, so it's usually under two hundred jobs. It loads in about a second from cold.

15
00:01:43,383 --> 00:01:50,213
Diego Alvarez: On iOS I'm reusing the same cache schema, so hopefully it's two or three days of work, not a week.

16
00:01:50,742 --> 00:01:55,087
Shreyas: Two or three days is fine. Nothing's waiting on it this week.

17
00:01:55,362 --> 00:01:58,697
Shreyas: Does that mean the offline list misses today's cut?

18
00:01:59,236 --> 00:02:09,451
Diego Alvarez: Yeah. Honestly it was never really going to make this one. I'd rather it goes out in next week's release with the real field than hack around it.

19
00:02:09,824 --> 00:02:15,574
Shreyas: Okay, agreed. Offline list goes in next week's release, not this one. Priya?

20
00:02:16,156 --> 00:02:28,476
Priya Nair: Yesterday was mostly SOC 2 prep. Kestrel Audit sent over their evidence request list, it's about sixty items, and I've mapped maybe two thirds of them to things we already collect.

21
00:02:28,684 --> 00:02:38,594
Priya Nair: Kestrel wants the observation window to start cleanly on the first of November, so everything on that list needs an owner by the end of next week.

22
00:02:38,956 --> 00:02:47,496
Priya Nair: I'll send each of you the handful of items that are yours on Monday. Most of it is screenshots of settings, nothing scary.

23
00:02:48,019 --> 00:02:50,849
Shreyas: Is anything on there going to surprise us?

24
00:02:51,472 --> 00:03:01,052
Priya Nair: Access reviews for the production database, probably. We've never done a formal one. I'll draft a process, but that's a next-week problem.

25
00:03:01,458 --> 00:03:12,238
Priya Nair: The other thing is the flaky test. The webhook retry integration test has failed something like one in eight runs this week, always on the timeout assertion.

26
00:03:12,585 --> 00:03:20,300
Priya Nair: I'm quarantining it this morning so it stops blocking merges, and I'll file a ticket with the logs I've got so far.

27
00:03:20,744 --> 00:03:23,199
Shreyas: Is it a real bug or just the test?

28
00:03:24,063 --> 00:03:37,703
Priya Nair: I think it's the test. It sleeps for a fixed two seconds and then checks the retry fired, and the CI runners are just slower some days. But I want to look properly before I say that for sure.

29
00:03:38,586 --> 00:03:47,186
Maya Chen: It does touch the retry queue I'm about to rewrite for v2, so I'm happy to pair on it next week if it turns out to be real.

30
00:03:47,855 --> 00:03:50,840
Priya Nair: Maybe. Let's see what the logs say first.

31
00:03:51,259 --> 00:04:02,779
Priya Nair: And today I'm driving the release cut. Plan's still Thursday afternoon, so four o'clock today. If you've got something that needs to be in, merge it by three thirty.

32
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:06,160
Shreyas: And the quarantined test won't block the cut?

33
00:04:06,727 --> 00:04:12,482
Priya Nair: No, quarantined tests still run but they don't gate anything. No blockers from me.

34
00:04:13,183 --> 00:04:15,618
Shreyas: Great, thanks. Tom, you're up.

35
00:04:16,347 --> 00:04:25,577
Tom Becker: Hey. So, queue-wise it's a lot calmer. We closed fourteen tickets yesterday, and nine of them were Fernhollow cleanup confirmations.

36
00:04:25,862 --> 00:04:35,307
Tom Becker: Owen replied this morning. He's on the release notes list now, his two dispatch leads too, and he asked when the postmortem is landing.

37
00:04:35,593 --> 00:04:44,438
Tom Becker: He also said his dispatchers have stopped double-checking every recurring job by hand, which, I think, is the real sign it's over.

38
00:04:45,024 --> 00:04:51,414
Shreyas: Still Friday. I'm finishing it tonight and I'll send it to Owen tomorrow, with you on copy.

39
00:04:51,934 --> 00:05:03,034
Tom Becker: Perfect. The other thing, there's a new ticket from one of the smaller plumbing accounts. One technician's jobs are showing an hour off in his Outlook calendar.

40
00:05:03,308 --> 00:05:12,483
Tom Becker: He's in a different time zone from his dispatcher, and I don't know yet if it's us or Microsoft. It's only the one technician so far.

41
00:05:12,845 --> 00:05:22,700
Maya Chen: Hmm, that sounds like the time zone on the series master, we've seen something like that before with recurring events. It might be the, um...

42
00:05:23,534 --> 00:05:29,644
Shreyas: Let's take that one offline. Maya, Tom, can you grab ten minutes straight after this?

43
00:05:30,258 --> 00:05:31,633
Maya Chen: Yep, works for me.

44
00:05:32,189 --> 00:05:37,574
Tom Becker: Sure, I'll send a huddle link right after. That's it from me, no blockers.

45
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:48,369
Tom Becker: Oh, and Noor and I might have the onboarding survey results by next week, depending on how many come back. She's out today, so I'm just flagging it.

46
00:05:49,230 --> 00:05:58,025
Shreyas: Me, quickly. Yesterday was one on ones and hiring. We've got two more senior backend screens on the calendar for next week.

47
00:05:58,197 --> 00:06:05,567
Shreyas: Today I'm on the Fernhollow postmortem, and I'll review Maya's renewal design once it's ready, no rush on that.

48
00:06:05,961 --> 00:06:16,511
Shreyas: And a reminder for everyone, Maya's off the on-call rotation for the next two weeks. I'm primary for anything sync related and Diego's secondary this weekend.

49
00:06:17,158 --> 00:06:22,398
Diego Alvarez: Yep, I've read the runbook twice. Please nobody break anything on Saturday.

50
00:06:23,265 --> 00:06:30,955
Shreyas: Oh, and someone floated moving standup to async on Fridays. I'm not deciding that today, just think about it.

51
00:06:31,841 --> 00:06:34,521
Diego Alvarez: I'd vote for that, for what it's worth.

52
00:06:34,896 --> 00:06:38,101
Priya Nair: I'm neutral. As long as people actually post.

53
00:06:38,962 --> 00:06:52,037
Shreyas: Noted. Okay, recap. Maya adds the field by end of day tomorrow, Priya quarantines the test and cuts at four, merge by three thirty, and Maya and Tom take the Outlook thing offline.

54
00:06:52,452 --> 00:06:54,827
Shreyas: Thanks, all. Have a good one.

55
00:06:55,573 --> 00:06:57,513
Priya Nair: Thanks, everyone, bye now.

56
00:06:57,934 --> 00:07:03,229
Diego Alvarez: Wait, quick one, did the office coffee machine die again or is it just me?

57
00:07:04,085 --> 00:07:09,290
Tom Becker: It's not dead, someone unplugged it for the vacuum. I'll plug it back in.

58
00:07:09,890 --> 00:07:11,320
Diego Alvarez: Later, see you all.
